{
  "packet_id": "44dd9fa28ffa1525",
  "dimensions": {
    "problem_framing": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 2,
      "event_ids": ["A1"],
      "reason": "A1 separates the objective from the suggested solution. It lists real alternatives: no expansion, licensing and partnering. It never names a specific use case, although the question asks for one. Alternative 2 is muddled: a 'B2B segment' that targets private boat owners. It also misses the premise a good analyst would check. The dossier shows Jotun already runs a consumer decorative business (Optimal, Multicolor Centers) and already sells leisure-yacht coatings direct to individuals. The €20,000 budget and 12-week limit are stated as assumptions, which is acceptable."
    },
    "causal_mechanism": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A9", "A10"],
      "reason": "T1, the best theory, names a benefit: trusted durability lowers purchase risk. It never explains which marine or protective technology property matters for which homeowner job. Value capture is a list ('subscription-based service contracts, and brand licensing') with no chain to margin for this manufacturer. It is also inconsistent with the 'cheaper than the competition' positioning the trace itself cites at A11."
    },
    "distinct_theories": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A9", "A10"],
      "reason": "T1 and T2 assume the same customer, the same product and the same core driver (brand trust producing a premium). They differ only in channel, online versus Multicolor Centers. They are rewordings of one adoption story. No real rival is offered, such as low homeowner demand, boat owners as the target, or a licensing route."
    },
    "assumptions_predictions": {
      "status": "scored",
      "score": 1,
      "event_ids": ["A9", "A10"],
      "reason": "Assumptions are stated. Several predictions are vague or not predictions at all, e.g. 'Brand reputation would be measured by repeat purchase intent'. The '15% of total Jotun revenue within 12 months' prediction is an arbitrary threshold with no link to the theory. Its failure would not clearly damage the specific mechanism."
    },
    "evidence_judgement": {
      "status": "scored",
